Wish from the CitiAI operators (2026-10-13): one call that answers 'what does this project cost right now, per hour and per month'. Inputs: all running servers (server_type price for the server's location), volumes (size x pricing.volume.price_per_gb_month), primary IPs (ipv4/ipv6 per location), floating IPs, load balancers. Output: table per resource (name, type, location, EUR/h, EUR/month) plus total; optional --label selector (e.g. citiai-env=live); --json. Library API too (e.g. $cloud->costs(label_selector => ...)), not only CLI. Note: Hetzner caps hourly billing at the monthly price; pricing.vat_rate may be 0 (net) — show which. Measured reference 2026-10-13 fsn1: cx23 0.0088/h 5.49/mo, cpx32 0.0569/h 35.49/mo, volume 0.0572/GB/mo, ipv4 0.0008/h 0.50/mo.

Implemented: WWW::Hetzner::Cloud::Costs + $cloud->costs(label_selector=>, price=>'gross'|'net') + hcloud.pl costs [--label] [--net] [--json]. Gross default, net/vat_rate exposed. Hourly for volume/floating IP derived as monthly/624 (Hetzner's hourly:monthly ratio for every dual-priced item), flagged hourly_derived. All servers counted regardless of status, plus server_backup rows (20%) when backup_window set. Unpriced primary IP types (ipv6) = 0; missing type/location -> undef price, warning, excluded from total. Fixed drift: live API returns 'location' (no 'datacenter') on servers and primary IPs; Server/PrimaryIP->location now read it (fallback datacenter.location), Server gains backup_window. prove -lr t/ green (60 files). Live read-only run OK. Drift for follow-up cards (this board): server list DATACENTER column and primary-ip datacenter_name show '-' against the live API since 'datacenter' is gone; label filter skips auto-created primary IPs without labels (by design, but surprising for operators).

